All four findings fixed, all four gates green.

**BLOCKER (#1)** — the requested edit (`fetch-depth: 0` in `.github/workflows/ci.yml`) **cannot be landed by this pipeline**. I made it and measured the consequence:

```
== diff hygiene
  FAIL forbidden path touched: .github/workflows/ci.yml
```

`rbops/verify.sh:176` forbids `.github/workflows/*` and AGENTS.md §1.1 forbids it outright. So I reverted it and fixed the blocker on the side that *is* in scope, in the direction the finding pointed:

- `ensure_full_history()` completes a shallow clone (`git fetch --unshallow`), then **reads the depth again and refuses if it's still short**. Not tolerance — a repair that fails is a loud refusal, never a pass.
- `resolve_main()` also fixed a *second* way the target was red: a pull-request CI checkout is a detached merge ref with **no local `main`**, so `git log main` was `fatal: ambiguous argument`.

Verified against three real clones with isolated builds: depth-1 push clone → 24 green (depth `true`→`false`); depth-1 PR shape with `refs/heads/main` deleted → 24 green; depth-1 clone with no remote → **4 red**, naming git's reason. Before the fix a depth-1 clone audits `0` checkpoints — the exact false pass.

The end-to-end run also caught a real race no fixture could: three tests fetched concurrently and collided on `.git/shallow.lock`. Now serialised behind `HISTORY_REPAIR`.

**MAJOR (#2)** — directive detection now tests `|` before `=`, so `deadbeef|a=b` is an entry. New `edge_an_equals_sign_in_a_reason_is_not_read_as_a_directive`; reverting the fix turns it red.

**MAJOR (#3)** — `stale_acknowledgements.is_empty()` is now asserted in `checkpoint_ancestry_on_main_is_acknowledged`. Appending `deadbeef|tolerated: junk` to the checked-in file now fails by name (it used to stay green).

**MINOR (#4)** — dropped the on-disk no-CR assertion (it coupled the test to `core.autocrlf`); kept and strengthened the LF/CRLF parse equality.

Gates: `cargo fmt --check` pass · `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings` pass, zero warnings · `cargo test --all-targets` 1510 passed / 0 failed · `verify.sh phase-078` **VERIFY PASS**, report-honesty check now exact (1510/1510).

`REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` §2 record that the one-line CI change is still the better fix and remains a human's to make — it is cheaper and keeps the network out of the suite. I have not committed anything.
